  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Redonda Restoration Programme: Ensuring the recovery and long-term protection of a unique assemblage of endangered species</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funds under this award are to be used to reverse the decline of the dozens of endemic and globally threatened species that inhabit the Redonda Island Key Biodiversity Area in Antigua and Barbuda, such as the Critically Endangered Redonda ground lizard, the Redonda anole, and the newly discovered Redonda pygmy gecko.</narrative>
  </description>
